  "summary": "A framework/controller interpretation mismatch undermined OAuth consent and earned USD 25,000.",
  "root_cause": "Routing and application logic disagreed about request semantics, allowing a state-changing operation outside its intended consent checks.",
  "impact": "Unauthorized OAuth grants could expose or modify private account data after user interaction.",
  "defensive_takeaways": [
    "Make state-changing handlers explicitly validate their permitted methods and consent.",
    "Verify that framework defaults preserve application security assumptions."
  ],
